{
  "_comment": "Per-pretext sender + landing-page playbook. Picks a lookalike/invented domain technique that fits each pretext (Neryss' table). Placeholders {brand} and {tld} are filled from the target's own domain (e.g. revel8.ai -> brand=revel8, tld=ai); {colleague} is filled from a network fact when we have one. All domains are registrable lookalikes an attacker could own; NEVER the target's real domain (the quality gate enforces that). Shared by writer.py and the frontend via /api/senders.",
  "techniques": {
    "invented_third_party": "A standalone org with no real brand to compare against — most believable for speaker/recruiter/press/investor/customer.",
    "vendor_lookalike": "Looks like a tool/vendor the target uses — invoices, document shares, auditors.",
    "cousin_brand": "{brand}-security.com / {brand}-hr.com — reads as an internal portal.",
    "typosquat": "{brand}-team.com or a 1-for-l swap — reads as an internal colleague.",
    "subdomain": "{brand}.{tld}.secure-login.com — strong for a sign-in (credentials) page."
  },
  "pretexts": {
